  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">217651 Education Cannot Wait (ECW) Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education Cannot Wait is a global fund dedication to education in emergencies and protracted crises. ECW fund a three-year Multi-Year Resilience Programme (MYRP) called &quot;Komeza Wige&quot;, providing a $12 million seed fund, equally co-led by UNICEF and WVUK/ WV Burundi ($6 million each). The seed fund refers to the expectation for all programme partners to fundraise throughout the programme with the aim of increasing the total budget to $30 million.
 
 Komeza Wige responds to the effects of conflict and crisis which have left 1.9 million school-age children and adolescents out of school. It aims to improve the continuity of education for vulnerable children and adolescents including those with disabilities, those who have been internally displaced, and former refugees who have recently returned home. Its holistic approach promotes learning for girls, boys, and adolescents, especially those at risk of dropping out of school, while improving their protection and well-being and reintegrating those who are out of school. The programme is implemented in two provinces: Cibitoke and Makamba; provinces with huge needs in education sector with few partners in education. 
 
 Key activities include the delivery of safe, protective and resilient learning spaces for children, support to teachers so they can deliver quality learning outcomes as well as mental health and psychosocial support, and a school-feeding component for children. 
 
 Overall, the MYRP aims to support 300,000 children and adolescents, including children and adolescents with disabilities (who comprise 10% of the total overall).
 
  
 
 Design team : Mainly made by UNICEF and World Vision plus strategic partner (Ministry of Education and UNESCO).</narrative>
  </description>
